#: ../../../how-to/pin-packages.rst:3
msgid "Pin packages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/pin-packages.rst:5
msgid ""
"Hold an installation at its current version so upgrades skip it until you "
"unpin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/pin-packages.rst:9
msgid "Pin it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/pin-packages.rst:11
msgid "$ pipx pin black"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/pin-packages.rst:15
msgid ""
"Pinned environments are skipped by ``pipx upgrade`` and ``pipx upgrade-"
"all``, so the app and its dependencies keep their versions until you unpin. "
"``pipx reinstall`` refuses a pinned environment, and ``pipx reinstall-all`` "
"reports it as an error. ``pipx install --force`` and ``pipx inject --force`` "
"keep a package pinned, even when they install a different version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/pin-packages.rst:20
msgid ""
"``pipx pin PACKAGE`` pins the main package and any injected packages in that "
"environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/pin-packages.rst:21
msgid ""
"``pipx pin PACKAGE --injected-only`` leaves the main package upgradable but "
"pins every injected package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/pin-packages.rst:22
msgid ""
"``pipx pin PACKAGE --skip PKG_A PKG_B`` pins injected packages except the "
"listed ones (implies ``--injected-only``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/pin-packages.rst:23
msgid ""
"``pipx unpin PACKAGE`` unpins the main package and every pinned injected "
"package in that environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/pin-packages.rst:25
msgid ""
"Pass ``--output json`` to read the changed and skipped packages from a "
"script, or ``--quiet`` to omit confirmations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/pin-packages.rst:29
msgid ""
"pipx pins the main package and injected packages, not individual transitive "
"dependencies. Pinning the main package freezes its whole dependency set, "
"because pipx skips ``pip install --upgrade`` for that environment. A package "
"injected after ``pipx pin`` starts unpinned, so ``pipx upgrade --include-"
"injected`` still upgrades it; run ``pipx pin PACKAGE`` again to pin it too. "
"For how pipx records this metadata, see :doc:`../explanation/how-pipx-works`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/pin-packages.rst:36
msgid "Verify it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/pin-packages.rst:38
msgid "$ pipx list --pinned"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/pin-packages.rst:42
msgid "Add ``--include-injected`` to also list pinned injected packages."
msgstr ""
